5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6cbe9eb8\" lines=\"79-94\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:12:Rebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:14:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:15:- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:16:- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:17:- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:18:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:19:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:20:- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:21:- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:22:- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:23:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:24:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:25:- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:26:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:27:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:28:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:29:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3d6c6e23\" lines=\"10-27\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:30:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:31:Move each vertical stream of pixels into a bottom-aligned centered pile.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:32:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:33:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:34:- A mostly background grid contains one or more vertical source columns of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:35:  foreground pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:36:- Each source column has n^2 foreground pixels, and the top-to-bottom color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:37:  sequence splits into monochrome groups of lengths 1, 3, 5, ...\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:38:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:39:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:40:- Clear the canvas to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:41:- For each source column, read the foreground colors from top to bottom and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:42:  rebuild them at the bottom below the same column as odd-width centered\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:43:  rows of lengths 1, 3, 5, ...\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:44:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:45:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:46:- The scattered vertical pixels are falling grains; a square number of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:47:  grains decomposes into the odd row widths of a centered pyramid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:48:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:49:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:50:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:51:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"c7f57c3e\" lines=\"22-35\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:52:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:53:Swap every sprite to the opposite prototype while preserving scale and position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:54:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:55:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:56:- bg = most common color. Two distinct small sprite patterns (prototypes) appear at various scales.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:57:- Each sprite instance is a scaled copy of one of the two prototypes, placed on the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:58:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:59:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:60:- Identify the two prototype patterns from the smallest-area sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:61:- For each sprite, determine which prototype it matches and its integer scale factor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:62:- Replace it with the other prototype at the same scale, aligned by an internal anchor region (color-1 pixels).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:63:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:64:Key insight: Every sprite toggles to the alternate prototype; the anchor sub-region inside each sprite pins the alignment so swapped sprites land in the correct position regardless of scale.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:65:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:66:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:67:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:68:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"269e22fb\" lines=\"46-60\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:69:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:70:Complete a visible crop into the shared 20x20 binary motif in its matching orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:71:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:72:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:73:- The grid is a two-color rectangular crop of one rotation/reflection of the same 20x20 motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:74:- One color is the motif foreground and the other color is the motif background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:75:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:76:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:77:- Try each input color as the foreground mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:78:- Match that mask against every possible window in every dihedral orientation of the motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:79:- Repaint the uniquely matched full 20x20 motif with the matched foreground/background colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:80:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:81:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:82:- The examples are partial windows of one canonical binary pattern; the local crop is distinctive enough to identify the full orientation and offset.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:83:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:84:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:85:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:86:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c920a713\" lines=\"87-102\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:87:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:88:Untangle overlapping colored rectangular frames into concentric square frames ordered by their visible crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:89:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:90:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:91:- The background contains several one-cell-thick axis-aligned rectangular frames, one color per frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:92:- Frames overlap, and the visible color at an overlap records a directed crossing from the hidden frame to the visible frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:93:- Each foreground color still has visible pixels on the perimeter of its full rectangular bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:94:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:95:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:96:- Infer each color's full rectangular frame from the bounding box of its visible pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:97:- Add a directed edge A -> B when B is visible at a crossing of A and B's frame perimeters.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:98:- Find the unique path that visits every frame color once, then render those colors as one-pixel-thick concentric square frames from outside to inside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:99:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:100:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:101:- The output is not a crop of the input; the crossing graph gives a single frame order, and that order is redrawn as nested rings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:102:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:103:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:104:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:105:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"abc82100\" lines=\"70-86\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:106:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:107:Use local source-target-pattern examples to replace matching source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:108:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:109:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:110:- Black background with isolated colored pixels and teal (8) pattern components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:111:- A rule example is a 4-neighbor colored pair source->target whose continued\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:112:  direction reaches an anchor touching a teal pattern component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:113:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:114:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:115:- For each rule example, copy that teal component onto every other pixel of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:116:  source.color, recoloring the copied component to target.color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:117:- Translation maps the rule anchor onto the source pixel being replaced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:118:- Remove teal components and all pixels used by rule examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:119:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:120:Key insight: The two adjacent colored pixels define the color substitution and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:121:the anchor point; the nearby teal component is the stencil that gets recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:122:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:123:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:124:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:125:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d93c6891\" lines=\"84-101\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:126:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:127:Move each gray bar into its adjacent orange rectangle as full stripes from the contacted edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:128:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:129:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:130:- The scene uses black outside space, yellow fill, gray one-cell-thick bars, and solid orange rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:131:- Each gray bar 4-touches exactly one orange rectangle; some orange rectangles have no touching gray bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:132:- Gray bars touching the same orange rectangle all have the same orientation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:133:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:134:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:135:- Recolor every original gray cell to yellow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:136:- For each orange rectangle touched by gray bars, count the gray cells assigned to that rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:137:- Horizontal gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange rows starting from the contacted top or bottom row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:138:- Vertical gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange columns starting from the contacted left or right column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:139:- Orange rectangles with no touching gray bar remain unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:140:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:141:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:142:- The gray pixels are not copied by shape; their count is transferred into the neighboring orange rectangle as edge-aligned row or column stripes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:143:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:144:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:145:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:146:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9968a131\" lines=\"10-27\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:147:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:148:Shift alternating two-color row bars so each row aligns to the topmost bar's color columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:149:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:150:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:151:- The dominant background surrounds horizontal two-pixel bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:152:- Every foreground row has exactly one adjacent bar using the same two colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:153:- The topmost bar gives the reference left/right column for each color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:154:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:155:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:156:- Keep bars whose left color is already in its reference column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:157:- For a reversed bar, shift the whole two-pixel bar horizontally until its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:158:  left color lands in that color's reference column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:159:- Background cells vacated by shifted bars become background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:160:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:161:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:162:- The rows are not recolored; each two-color bar is translated so equal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:163:  colors line up with the topmost reference bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:164:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:165:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:166:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:167:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5751f35e\" lines=\"29-43\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:168:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:169:Complete sparse nested rectangular color layers into solid rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:170:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:171:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:172:The background is the dominant color, and every foreground color marks one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:173:axis-aligned rectangular layer; the layer bboxes have unique areas and are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:174:nested from outermost to innermost.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:175:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:176:Take each color's bbox as its completed rectangle, except that a child bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:177:which already matches at least three sides of its parent's one-pixel inset\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:178:expands to that full inset; repaint the rectangles largest to smallest.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:179:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:180:The scattered pixels are samples of nested rectangular regions, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:181:output is a clean redraw of those regions with inner colors overwriting\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:182:outer colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:183:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:184:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:185:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:186:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"800d221b\" lines=\"7-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:187:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:188:Recolor a path-network by adjacent seed regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:189:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:190:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:191:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:192:- Path color P forms a thin orthogonal network with a solid square hub (NxN).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:193:- Seed colors appear in colored regions (non-bg, non-P) adjacent to path branches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:194:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:195:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:196:- Infer P as the non-bg color whose largest component is most network-like.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:197:- Find the largest solid k×k all-P square (the hub); exclude it from recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:198:- Recolor each path branch to the seed-region color it touches most.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:199:- Recolor the hub center pixel to the seed whose branches touch the hub most.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:200:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:201:Key insight: The hub stays uncolored; branches inherit color from adjacent seed regions by adjacency count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:202:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:203:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:204:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:205:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4c7dc4dd\" lines=\"7-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:206:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:207:Learn a transformation rule from a training pair of framed sprites, then apply it to a test sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:208:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:209:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:210:- Grid contains several colored square frames (hollow borders of a single color).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:211:- Each frame's interior holds a small pattern sprite; one frame's interior is blank (all black).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:212:- Two frames form a training pair (their interiors share the same color palette); one remaining frame is the test case.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:213:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:214:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:215:- Identify the training pair by matching interior color sets; the other non-blank frame is the test input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:216:- Infer the rule mapping source→destination (e.g. reflection, color inversion, gap filling, endpoint extraction, or checkerboard complement).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:217:- Apply that same rule to the test sprite; output the transformed interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:218:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:219:Key insight: The puzzle is an analogy — \"A is to B as C is to ?\" — where you must discover the visual rule from one example pair and generalize it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:220:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:221:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:222:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:223:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"5545f144\" lines=\"191-207\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:224:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:225:Move a triangular sprite across the grid, consuming aligned marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:226:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:227:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:228:- Frames concatenated horizontally with solid divider columns; bg is most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:229:- Each frame: a triangular arrow-shaped sprite and scattered single-pixel markers, all one color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:230:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:231:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:232:- Start from the rightmost frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:233:- At each step, exactly one cardinal direction from the head has reachable\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:234:  markers (on a half-line: same row or column); the sprite advances to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:235:  nearest one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:236:- On reaching a marker, consume it; sprite re-faces that direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:237:- Repeat until no markers remain; output the final sprite position on a clean bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:238:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:239:Key insight: The triangle's tip encodes facing direction, which sets marker-consumption priority.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:240:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:241:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:242:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:243:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a25697e4\" lines=\"9-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:244:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:245:Dock movable tools into border-anchored frames by filling cavities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:246:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:247:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:248:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:249:- Border-touching components cluster into anchor frames with interior bg cavities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:250:- Non-border 2-color components are movable tools.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:251:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:252:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:253:- Match each tool to a frame whose cavity size equals one of its color-region counts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:254:- Rotate/flip the tool so one color fills the cavity exactly; the other stays outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:255:- If the docking orientation uses a reflection, swap the tool's two colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:256:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:257:Key insight: Cavity size determines tool–frame pairing; reflection triggers color swap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:258:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:259:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:260:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:261:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6350f1f4\" lines=\"62-81\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:262:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:263:Decode a block-grid image by swapping each sprite-coded cell with a solid cell and each blank cell with the sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:264:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:265:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:266:The grid is partitioned by black separator rows and columns into equal-size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:267:square blocks. Each block is either a copy of one two-color sprite or a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:268:uniform blank block of the sprite's minority color; grey pixels are erased\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:269:cells that act as wildcards.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:270:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:271:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:272:Infer the repeated sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks. Replace a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:273:block matching that sprite, ignoring grey erasures, with a solid block of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:274:the sprite's majority color. Replace a uniform blank block with the sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:275:Separator rows and columns, including grey erasures on them, become black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:276:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:277:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:278:The small sprite is a block-level code for one macro-cell state, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:279:uniform minority-color block is the other state; the output renders the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:280:opposite code in each macro-cell while cleaning erased pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:281:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:282:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:283:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:284:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"13e47133\" lines=\"56-69\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:285:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:286:Fill partitioned regions with concentric colored bands derived from marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:287:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:288:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:289:- Grid partitioned into regions by wall-colored lines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:290:- Each region has a dominant base color and a few isolated marker pixels of other colors at varying depths from the region boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:291:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:292:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:293:- For each region, read marker colors ordered by their Chebyshev distance from the boundary to build a color palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:294:- If no marker sits on the boundary itself, the base color leads the palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:295:- Paint every cell with palette[distance mod palette_length], producing repeating concentric rectangular frames that radiate inward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:296:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:297:Key insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:298:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:299:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:300:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:301:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"abbfd121\" lines=\"56-74\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:302:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:303:Recover the repeating background pattern hidden under the largest solid rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:304:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:305:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:306:- The grid is covered by a small row/column periodic pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:307:- Several non-pattern colors form solid rectangular foreground objects that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:308:  overwrite the pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:309:- The requested output region is the largest of those solid rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:310:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:311:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:312:- Find every 4-connected monochromatic object whose bounding box is a filled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:313:  rectangle with both dimensions greater than one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:314:- Treat those rectangles as masks, infer the smallest repeating tile that is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:315:  consistent with all remaining visible pixels, and repaint the largest\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:316:  rectangle's coordinates with that tile.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:317:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:318:Key insight: The rectangle colors are occluders; the visible pixels outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:319:them are enough to reconstruct the original periodic background underneath.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:320:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:321:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:322:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:323:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d968ffd4\" lines=\"15-28\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:324:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:325:Extend each of two aligned rectangular marker objects toward the other, filling half of the gap across the full perpendicular span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:326:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:327:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:328:- A dominant background contains exactly two solid, same-sized monochromatic rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:329:- The rectangles share either the same row span or the same column span, with a background gap between their facing edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:330:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:331:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:332:- If the rectangles are side-by-side, color the left half of the inter-object gap across every row with the left object's color, and the right half with the right object's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:333:- If one rectangle is above the other, color the upper half of the gap across every column with the upper object's color, and the lower half with the lower object's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:334:- When the gap length is odd, leave the center row/column as background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:335:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:336:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:337:- The marker objects are endpoints of an axial corridor; their own size identifies the facing edge, while the filled corridor spans the whole grid perpendicular to that axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:338:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:339:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:340:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:341:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bc93ec48\" lines=\"48-63\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:342:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:343:Copy each foreground object anchored in a true grid corner clockwise into the next corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:344:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:345:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:346:- The dominant color is the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:347:- Foreground objects are monochromatic 4-connected components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:348:- Relevant objects are exactly those whose bounding box touches two adjacent borders at one grid corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:349:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:350:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:351:- Start from the input unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:352:- For each corner object, copy its pixel mask and color to the next corner clockwise: top-left to top-right, top-right to bottom-right, bottom-right to bottom-left, and bottom-left to top-left.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:353:- Preserve each object's orientation by aligning its bounding box to the destination corner; stamps may overwrite existing pixels at the destination, but source pixels are not cleared.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:354:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:355:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:356:- Interior and side-only objects are distractors; only components actually anchored to a corner participate in the clockwise perimeter copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:357:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:358:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:359:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:360:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"46c35fc7\" lines=\"21-34\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:361:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:362:Rotate the colors around every 3x3 foreground ring, with corners and side-centers cycling in opposite directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:363:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:364:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:365:- The grid has a dominant background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:366:- Each 4-connected foreground object is a complete 3x3 ring: eight foreground pixels around a background center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:367:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:368:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:369:- For each ring, move corner colors one step around the four corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:370:- Move side-center colors one step around the four side centers in the opposite direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:371:- Leave the background center and all other background pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:372:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:373:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:374:- Corners and side centers form two separate four-cycles on the same 3x3 ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:375:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:376:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:377:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:378:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"58c02a16\" lines=\"10-26\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:379:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:380:Expand the top-left seed mask into a recursive colored pattern and tile it across the full grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:381:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:382:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:383:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:384:- All foreground lies in a top-left rectangle whose last row and last column are a solid secondary color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:385:- Removing that secondary-color row and column leaves a seed region containing background plus one primary color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:386:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:387:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:388:- Use the primary-color pixels in the seed as a binary mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:389:- Replace each primary seed cell with a copy of the seed mask in the primary color, and each background seed cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:390:  with a copy of the seed mask in the secondary color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:391:- Repeat and crop that expanded tile to the original grid shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:392:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:393:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:394:The solid L-shaped secondary-color border is a legend, not output content; it supplies the color used when the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:395:seed's background cells are expanded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:396:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:397:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:398:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:399:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:400:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:401:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:402:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:403:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:404:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:405:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:406:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:407:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:408:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:409:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:410:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:411:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:412:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:413:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:414:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:415:请一次性生成5个`<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:416:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:417:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:418:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:419:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:420:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:421:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:422:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:423:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:424:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:425:6. 新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:426:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:427:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:428:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:429:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:430:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:431:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:432:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:433:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:434:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:435:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:436:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:437:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:438:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:439:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:440:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:441:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:442:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:443:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用的复杂计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/prompt.md:444:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:1:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:2:- `description`：根据框架内部的\"钥匙\"形状选择对应的\"锁孔\"框架，将钥匙旋转后插入锁孔完成拼合，并用钥匙的颜色重绘整个锁孔框架的边框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:3:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:4:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:5:  - 背景为 Black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:6:  - 网格中散布着若干由单一颜色绘制的矩形空心框架（边框宽度为 1 像素），每个框架内部为 Black 背景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:7:  - 部分框架内部含有一个由另一种颜色绘制的小型连通形状（称为\"钥匙\"），钥匙形状不对称，占据框架内部的某个角落。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:8:  - 其余框架内部没有钥匙，但框架的某一条边上有一个连续缺口（若干连续像素缺失），缺口形状恰好能被某把钥匙经过 0/90/180/270 度旋转后精确填入。这类框架称为\"锁孔框架\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:9:  - 每把钥匙恰好匹配一个锁孔框架的缺口（按形状匹配），不存在歧义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:10:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:11:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:12:  - 第一步：对每把钥匙，遍历四个旋转角度，找到唯一一个锁孔框架，使得钥匙旋转后的轮廓恰好填满该框架边框上的缺口。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:13:  - 第二步：将旋转后的钥匙像素填入锁孔框架的缺口位置，补全框架边框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:14:  - 第三步：将该锁孔框架的整个边框颜色改为钥匙的颜色。原来包含钥匙的框架保持不变（钥匙从原框架中移除，原框架只剩空心边框）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:15:  - 输出网格尺寸与输入相同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:16:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:17:- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现\"钥匙\"和\"锁孔\"的形状匹配关系（需要尝试旋转），再发现匹配成功后框架颜色会被钥匙颜色覆盖——这是两层独立的非平凡推理：第一层是空间形状的旋转匹配，第二层是颜色传递规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:18:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:19:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:20:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:21:- `description`：将网格中散落的同色像素簇识别为\"种子\"，根据种子簇的像素数量决定其生长层数，向外逐层扩展形成同心矩形环带，不同种子的环带相遇时由像素数量更多的种子占据争议区域。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:22:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:23:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:24:  - 背景为 Black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:25:  - 网格中有若干个由不同颜色构成的小型 4-连通像素簇（每簇 2-6 个像素），各簇之间保持一定距离。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:26:  - 每个簇的颜色唯一（不同簇颜色不同）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:27:  - 簇的形状不规则，但每个簇都能被一个紧贴的矩形边界框包围。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:28:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:29:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:30:  - 对每个簇，计算其包含的像素数量 N。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:31:  - 以该簇的边界框为起始区域，向外扩展 N 层（每层在上下左右各扩展 1 像素，形成同心矩形环带），所有扩展层都用该簇的颜色填充。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:32:  - 簇本身的像素保持不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:33:  - 当两个不同簇的扩展区域在同一个像素上产生冲突时，像素数量更多的簇获胜，占据该像素。若像素数量相同，则保持 Black（不填充）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:34:  - 超出网格边界的扩展被裁剪。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:35:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:36:- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要发现每个簇的像素数量决定了其\"生长半径\"（数量即层数），然后需要发现冲突区域的归属规则——大簇优先覆盖小簇。这两层规则都需要通过对比多个样例中不同大小簇的扩展结果来归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:37:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:38:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:39:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:40:- `description`：网格被分割线划分为若干矩形房间，每个房间内有一个彩色箭头指示方向；将每个房间中的箭头沿其指向\"推送\"到相邻房间，被推入的房间接收箭头的颜色作为整个房间的填充色，而箭头原来所在的房间则用其特殊\"门色\"边界的颜色填充。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:41:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:42:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:43:  - 网格由 Grey 色的单像素宽分割线划分为若干矩形房间（类似网格状布局，但房间大小可以不等）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:44:  - 每个房间的内部背景为 Black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:45:  - 每个房间内恰好有一个由非 Black、非 Grey 颜色绘制的箭头形状。箭头由一条 1 像素宽的直线段（长度 2-4 像素）和末端的一个像素构成 T 形或 L 形尖端，指向上、下、左、右四个方向之一。箭头的朝向通过尖端像素相对于线段的位置来确定：尖端像素位于线段延长线方向上。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:46:  - 分割线将房间的边界着色为 Grey，但某些房间的某条边界上，分割线被替换为另一种非 Grey 的颜色（称为\"门色\"），长度覆盖该边界的全部。每个房间至多有一条边界带有门色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:47:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:48:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:49:  - 第一步：确定每个箭头的朝向（上/下/左/右）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/9/des.md:50:  - 第二步：检查箭头所指方向上，该房间是否存